  "_comment": "DRAFT — hand-authored route, v0.7.6 proposal §3 (Tier A). Review line-by-line before copying to the harness root as `.plugin-efficiency.json`. Rates, models, and thresholds are pinned against `references/MODEL_ALLOCATION.md §2` and `CLAUDE.md §12.9` (capability-inversion refusal floor). The `input_tokens_per_second` figure is a PLACEHOLDER pending a measured-throughput calibration on current-generation Opus 4.7 / Sonnet 4.6 connections; see §Honesty notes at the end of this object. The calibrator schema supports a binary `executor` / `orchestrator` tier split; Haiku 4.5 (at Reflector-lightweight per MODEL_ALLOCATION.md §2 on a 30-day pilot, H-MA-2) is NOT representable in this file and is documented in the README alongside. Duplication threshold is intentionally relaxed to 0.5 because the shared Grounding-Protocol quotations across agent prompts are not sprawl.",

